---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Sources from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/Sources.astro";
import { md as _md } from "../lib/md.js";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import all from "../data/sources.json";
const blurb = {
  Archive: "Places that hold the original paper, and that will copy it for you if you write.",
  Database: "Indexes and image collections searched online.",
  Portal: "Open gateways to whole bodies of scholarship or press — free, and the ones that actually let this archive in.",
  Publication: "Books, articles and dissertations — including several written by members of this family.",
  Transcription: "Published texts of works this archive otherwise reads only as page images.",
  Index: "Aggregated name indexes: useful for finding a person, never sufficient for proving one.",
  Reference: "Standing works of reference consulted for particular facts.",
  Family: "What the family itself holds: photographs, charts, a reunion album, and a website.",
  "Family file": "The family's own compiled files — genealogy software, exports and document scans.",
  "Online tree": "Trees published by other researchers. Read for leads, never taken as proof.",
};
/* Sections are derived from the data, in this order, and anything with a new
   kind is appended rather than silently dropped. */
const order = ["Archive", "Portal", "Database", "Index", "Publication", "Transcription",
               "Reference", "Family", "Family file", "Online tree"];
const present = [...new Set(all.map(s => s.kind))];
const kinds = [...order.filter(k => present.includes(k)),
               ...present.filter(k => !order.includes(k))];

/* 21 September 2026. This archive's row IS the kit's row — the component was
   built from this page in the first place, because of the one measurement
   that settled it: of 208 sources across the estate, 58 linked to the thing
   itself and all 58 were here. So this is not an adaptation, it is the
   original going back to where it was promoted to, and the page keeps only
   what is its own: the `kind` vocabulary, its order, and the sentence under
   each heading saying what that kind of thing is.

   The facets are the component's now too. They were this page's idea. */
const groups = kinds.map(k => ({
  label: k,
  note: blurb[k] || "Other material this archive rests on.",
  rows: all.filter(s => s.kind === k).map(s => ({
    id: s.id, title: s.title, url: s.url, where: s.where,
    what: _md(s.what), cites: s.cites, note: s.note ? _md(s.note) : null,
    held: s.held,
  })),
}));
const reach = all.filter(s => s.url).length;

/* THE KIND VOCABULARY IS DRIFTING AND THE FACET BAR NOW SHOWS IT. Ten kinds
   were intended and `blurb` above still defines exactly those ten. The data
   holds twenty-two, because one-offs have been typed straight into rows —
   "article", "book", "chapter", "Printed, 1845", "Archive, Trieste" — and
   one pair differs only in case, `Archive` and `archive`, which no reader
   can tell apart and no filter can join.
   Counted rather than folded. Folding them is a decision about what each
   source IS, and that belongs in the data with somebody who knows, not in a
   template quietly merging two labels because they look similar. */
const defined = Object.keys(blurb);
const undefined_ = kinds.filter(k => !defined.includes(k));
const caseDupes = kinds.filter(k =>
  kinds.some(o => o !== k && o.toLowerCase() === k.toLowerCase()));
const held = all.filter(s => !s.url && s.held).length;
---
<Base
  title="Sources"
  eyebrow={`${all.length} sources`}
  dek="Everything this archive is built on, what each one actually gave, and where each one is weak. Every page carries a block linking back to the entries here that it rests on.">

  <section class="prose">
    <p>An archive that will not say where it got something is a rumour with a stylesheet. This page is the answer to “how do you know that?”, and it is meant to be usable: where a source can be written to, its address is here; where it can be searched, the link is live; where it is wrong or thin, that is said in the entry rather than buried.</p>
    <p>Three of these sources conflict with others on points of fact. In every case this archive prefers the contemporaneous register over the later family memory, says so on the page where the conflict appears, and leaves the question open rather than quietly picking a winner.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:22px"><strong>{reach} of the {all.length} link to the thing
  itself</strong>, {held} are paper this family holds and say where, and {all.length - reach - held}
  carry neither — scholarly books and articles where choosing the right edition is research and a
  wrong link is worse than none.</p>
  {undefined_.length > 0 && (
    <p class="cap"><strong>{kinds.length} kinds, and {defined.length} of them were the vocabulary.</strong>
    {" "}{undefined_.length} have been typed straight into a row and have no definition on this page:
    <em>{undefined_.join(", ")}</em>.
    {caseDupes.length > 0 && <> Two differ only in case — <em>{caseDupes.join(" and ")}</em> — which
    no reader can tell apart and no filter can join.</>}
    {" "}They are counted here rather than quietly merged, because folding them is a decision about
    what each source <em>is</em>.</p>
  )}

  {/* `u` is deliberately NOT passed. The component prefixes the site base onto
      hrefs written into source data by hand, which is right for the archives
      that hold raw HTML — but this archive's md() already bases every link it
      renders, so passing it produced /TheDefranceski/TheDefranceski/research-log/.
      Caught by the link checker, which is exactly the fault it exists for. */}
  <div style="margin-top:20px"><Sources groups={groups} /></div>

  <section class="prose" style="margin-top:48px">
    <h3>What was deliberately not done</h3>
    <p>The Antenati search at the Italian state archives sits behind a bot check, and it was not bypassed. FamilySearch's images were not bulk-downloaded: their terms do not permit it, and seventeenth- to nineteenth-century secretary hand defeats optical character recognition anyway. Commercial heraldry sites were read for leads and their pictures were not reproduced. No image of a living person appears anywhere on this site.</p>
    <h3>If you want to check something</h3>
    <p>Start with the page it appears on — each carries its own source block — then come here for the address. The two archives most worth writing to are <a href={u("/sources/#dapa")}>Pazin</a>, which answered this family twice in 2021 for about a hundred kuna a time, and <a href={u("/sources/#arolsen")}>Arolsen</a>, which is free.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<!-- The filter script that used to live here is gone with the markup it
     drove. It queried .filters and .kindsec, which this page no longer has;
     the kit component carries the same behaviour, having taken the idea from
     this page when it was promoted. A listener bound to selectors that no
     longer exist is not harmless — it is a dead thing that looks alive. -->

